01:26:01.856 --> 01:26:05.176
Kenzo: Traveler, what brings you to Ravenshold, or why are you headed to Ravenshold?

01:26:06.936 --> 01:26:14.716
Riswynn: So my name is Riswynn, and I live in, uh, the Yuvanti Mountains in the city of Tharn Todor.

01:26:14.716 --> 01:26:20.636
Riswynn: And I am on a quest, uh, for the benefit of my clan.

01:26:20.636 --> 01:26:30.916
Riswynn: Um, I don't know what you've heard or what your connection is to Raven's Claw, but, uh, we dwarves are aware that, uh, there are some rumors that dwarvish artifacts

01:26:30.916 --> 01:26:35.476
Riswynn: are disappearing into the west, and of course we don't approve.

01:26:35.476 --> 01:26:45.596
Riswynn: And, and there are people, uh, there, there are dwarves who've manned a, a larger quest to sort of retrieve a, a massive, a massive

01:26:45.596 --> 01:26:55.636
Riswynn: push of restoring things that we had left behind in our exodus from, uh, the Central Mountains when we moved down to the, to, uh, the Ardet,

01:26:55.636 --> 01:26:58.176
Riswynn: um, and the Yuvanti.

01:26:58.176 --> 01:27:00.956
Riswynn: And so we, uh,

01:27:02.156 --> 01:27:09.616
Riswynn: Brawn, well, Brawn anvils have, uh, a connection to Ravensholt, and one of our family artifacts is there.

01:27:09.616 --> 01:27:16.796
Riswynn: And since it's so far to the east, uh, it might be one of the last things collected or even forgotten entirely by the main dwarvish party.

01:27:16.796 --> 01:27:24.775
Riswynn: So my clan has sent me to recover, um, this, uh, artifact of our clan.

01:27:28.836 --> 01:27:35.316
Riswynn: Though I've heard that there is some troubling, uh, violence and unsafety in this region.

01:27:35.316 --> 01:27:45.036
Riswynn: And so I thought instead of just continuing my quest, uh, solo to Ravensholt, it might be wise to seek some traveling companions.

01:27:49.056 --> 01:27:50.916
Seeker: That is all very fascinating information.

01:27:54.176 --> 01:27:56.136
DM: [laughs]

01:27:56.136 --> 01:27:58.996
Seeker: Uh, I'm Seeker. I come from, uh, Highkeep.

01:27:58.996 --> 01:28:00.276
Seeker: I'm Seeker of Highkeep. Way,

01:28:01.316 --> 01:28:07.096
Seeker: uh, far, far to the north of, of here is, is my, uh, family's, uh, holdings.

01:28:08.556 --> 01:28:09.916
Seeker: Um, I've

01:28:11.416 --> 01:28:20.116
Seeker: come this way south on my own spiritual journey, but fallen in with this band of interesting folks trying to do what we can to protect the peoples of this, of this area.

01:28:21.176 --> 01:28:23.276
Riswynn: Did you keep to the mountains on your journey south?

01:28:23.276 --> 01:28:28.556
Riswynn: Or ha- like, have you already been to the Ravensholt area?

01:28:28.556 --> 01:28:33.536
Seeker: Um, I have not been through there, uh, nor have the rest of us.

01:28:33.536 --> 01:28:35.236
Seeker: Is that true? No.

01:28:35.236 --> 01:28:37.016
Seeker: None of us have, have been nearby.

01:28:38.256 --> 01:28:38.456
Seeker: Uh,

01:28:40.916 --> 01:28:46.156
Seeker: I'm very interested to learn more about these artifacts, but perhaps we can discuss along the way.

01:28:46.156 --> 01:28:46.996
Seeker: I, I was

01:28:48.316 --> 01:28:50.356
Seeker: gifted just recently

01:28:51.756 --> 01:28:57.836
Seeker: a book, but I do not know who gave the gift or what the origin is of the book.

01:28:57.836 --> 01:29:00.276
Seeker: Does that sound familiar?

01:29:00.276 --> 01:29:01.636
Riswynn: No.

01:29:01.636 --> 01:29:02.796
Riswynn: [laughs]

01:29:02.856 --> 01:29:06.656
Seeker: It is a, a book of runes, the runes of our people.

01:29:07.876 --> 01:29:09.516
Riswynn: Runes are very significant

01:29:11.036 --> 01:29:12.455
Riswynn: to, to all of us, of course.

01:29:12.456 --> 01:29:12.615
Riswynn: Um,

01:29:13.736 --> 01:29:18.376
Riswynn: I only have particular knowledge of a, of a few myself, but, uh,

01:29:19.656 --> 01:29:21.796
Riswynn: I can see that the book would be a, a treasure.

01:29:21.796 --> 01:29:25.936
Riswynn: It's, uh, impressive that something just landed in your lap.

01:29:27.096 --> 01:29:29.156
Seeker: It's, it's quite a beautiful artifact.

01:29:29.156 --> 01:29:29.896
Seeker: I, I take it out

01:29:30.916 --> 01:29:35.356
Seeker: and j- I don't open the book itself, but just to, to, to show off the-

01:29:35.356 --> 01:29:45.036
DM: It is, I mean, it's very nice. It's like the, the cover itself is like almost made of, of stone, like very finely polished granite with this like...

01:29:45.036 --> 01:29:55.115
DM: And it has in dwarven runes, [coughs] the title is The Runes of Creation, sort of carved in elaborate inlaid letters with like little traces of silver and stuff

01:29:55.115 --> 01:29:55.596
DM: like that.

01:29:58.016 --> 01:30:05.996
Seeker: I've, I've already learned a great deal from the deep study of this book, which caused me to unfortunately miss a few of the Axbeek races, but it was worthwhile.

01:30:10.956 --> 01:30:13.696
Riswynn: I'm, I'm impressed. It looks, it looks very

01:30:15.456 --> 01:30:17.016
Riswynn: exciting.

01:30:17.016 --> 01:30:20.886
Seeker: [laughs] I'd, I'd hope to learn more about where it came from, but

01:30:21.996 --> 01:30:23.076
Seeker: we'll see what we can find out.

01:30:25.696 --> 01:30:27.596
Kenzo: Hey, Wellby, look at your messages.

01:30:32.956 --> 01:30:33.196
Seeker: Um...

01:30:36.326 --> 01:30:40.996
Riswynn: So when are you s- are you staying through the festival and then preparing for your journey?

01:30:40.996 --> 01:30:45.576
Riswynn: Or what, what is your reason for going to Ravensholt and your timeframe?

01:30:47.736 --> 01:30:51.356
Seeker: [festive music] Peak in the music.

01:30:51.356 --> 01:30:54.956
Seeker: Uh, we, uh, we, we had thought to leave after the festival.

01:30:56.816 --> 01:30:57.156
DM: It is a

01:30:58.496 --> 01:31:00.776
Delwath: very dangerous time to be traveling by yourself.

