DM: Uh, bonus action?

02:58:01.088 --> 02:58:03.128
Delwath: Mm, I'm not gonna... I don't think I'm gonna bother.

02:58:04.208 --> 02:58:04.508
DM: Okay.

02:58:05.568 --> 02:58:09.128
DM: Um, okay, so this thing's still asleep.

02:58:10.628 --> 02:58:11.748
DM: And, um,

02:58:13.568 --> 02:58:13.738
DM: uh,

02:58:15.668 --> 02:58:25.688
DM: uh, Wellby, as Ander, um, starts running and looks down at his feet, you just hear this stream of, "No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no,

02:58:25.688 --> 02:58:27.008
DM: no, no, no, no, no."

02:58:28.488 --> 02:58:28.908
Unknown: [laughs]

02:58:28.908 --> 02:58:31.448
DM: And he faints.

02:58:31.448 --> 02:58:32.088
Unknown: Oh.

02:58:32.088 --> 02:58:33.338
Unknown: Wow.

02:58:33.338 --> 02:58:33.368
Unknown: [laughs]

02:58:33.368 --> 02:58:34.668
Unknown: Well done.

02:58:34.668 --> 02:58:36.108
Unknown: Thanks. [laughs]

02:58:36.108 --> 02:58:38.028
Unknown: Total success.

02:58:38.028 --> 02:58:39.808
DM: Uh, and now it is your turn again.

02:58:41.448 --> 02:58:43.288
Seeker: Oh, it's my turn again?

02:58:43.288 --> 02:58:45.418
DM: It's... Yeah, 'cause we skipped your turn last time, so now it's back to-

02:58:45.418 --> 02:58:46.538
Unknown: Oh, right, right, right

02:58:46.538 --> 02:58:46.538
DM: ... it's your turn again

02:58:46.538 --> 02:58:48.148
Unknown: ... happens fast.

02:58:48.148 --> 02:58:48.198
DM: Yeah.

02:58:48.198 --> 02:58:48.628
Unknown: Um,

02:58:50.988 --> 02:58:52.888
Seeker: there's not much left for me to do.

02:58:52.888 --> 02:58:54.488
Seeker: Does anybody need healing again?

02:58:57.008 --> 02:58:57.488
Unknown: Um,

02:58:58.788 --> 02:59:03.968
Delwath: Delwath could... You... I mean, I'm at h- I only have 10 hit points left, but I, I think this guy's gonna die soon.

02:59:05.628 --> 02:59:08.088
Delwath: But I could only take one... I couldn't take even another hit.

02:59:09.388 --> 02:59:13.408
Seeker: Oh, yeah. I'll, I'll send some healing vibes.

02:59:17.348 --> 02:59:18.888
Unknown: That's four.

02:59:18.888 --> 02:59:20.388
Kenzo: Ah, healing's so useful.

02:59:20.388 --> 02:59:20.448
Unknown: Help.

02:59:20.448 --> 02:59:21.528
Unknown: Jeez.

02:59:21.528 --> 02:59:23.188
Unknown: Yeah, yeah.

02:59:23.188 --> 02:59:27.648
Kenzo: We've taken a huge amount of aggregate damage this, this, this battle, like lots-

02:59:27.648 --> 02:59:27.698
Unknown: It-

02:59:27.698 --> 02:59:29.368
Kenzo: ... and lots of damage.

02:59:29.368 --> 02:59:32.128
Seeker: Yeah. With the exception of those of us who prudently-

02:59:32.128 --> 02:59:33.108
DM: Chose to hide away

02:59:33.108 --> 02:59:34.567
Unknown: ... ran into the building. [laughs]

02:59:34.568 --> 02:59:34.808
DM: Yeah.

02:59:34.808 --> 02:59:35.748
Unknown: [laughs]

02:59:35.748 --> 02:59:38.088
Riswynn: Stood in front of the monsters with some fancy armor on.

02:59:38.088 --> 02:59:39.948
Unknown: [laughs] That's true.

02:59:39.948 --> 02:59:42.048
DM: Riswynn hasn't taken any hits yet.

02:59:42.048 --> 02:59:44.148
Seeker: That's interesting. Yeah, good armor, I guess.

02:59:44.148 --> 02:59:44.588
Unknown: Impressive.

02:59:47.068 --> 02:59:49.188
DM: Uh, a- that's your bonus action.

02:59:49.188 --> 02:59:50.568
DM: Are you doing anything else with your action?

02:59:51.868 --> 02:59:52.128
Unknown: Um,

02:59:53.788 --> 02:59:55.978
Seeker: I can't, I can't think of anything to do, so I'm...

02:59:55.978 --> 02:59:57.568
Unknown: I'll just chill.

02:59:58.788 --> 02:59:59.008
DM: Okay.

03:00:00.068 --> 03:00:00.628
DM: Uh, Riswynn.

03:00:02.468 --> 03:00:06.848
Riswynn: All right. I'm just going to, um, whack at the thing with my war hammer.

03:00:10.888 --> 03:00:12.898
Unknown: Whack.

03:00:14.388 --> 03:00:15.048
Unknown: Yes.

03:00:15.048 --> 03:00:16.128
DM: Um, that hits.

03:00:17.148 --> 03:00:17.347
Unknown: Boom.

03:00:17.348 --> 03:00:19.868
DM: And with that strike,

03:00:20.928 --> 03:00:21.148
DM: um,

03:00:22.388 --> 03:00:26.847
DM: you smash it, and it just kind of collapses again, and you hear this...

03:00:26.848 --> 03:00:36.608
DM: Again, you hear, like, a, a sizzling and, um, a bit of a, of a, of this sort of mad yelping as it

03:00:38.548 --> 03:00:40.028
DM: crashes to the ground dead.

03:00:43.308 --> 03:00:44.688
DM: Okay.

03:00:44.688 --> 03:00:46.868
DM: This thing's still asleep.

03:00:46.868 --> 03:00:50.228
DM: You have probably another 30 seconds before it wakes up.

03:00:50.228 --> 03:00:50.848
Unknown: Oh, jeez.

03:00:53.148 --> 03:00:53.908
Unknown: But I'm not-

03:00:53.908 --> 03:00:55.128
DM: I'm not gonna bother with initiative at this point.

03:00:55.128 --> 03:00:57.148
DM: What do you wanna do?

03:00:57.148 --> 03:01:00.228
Riswynn: Well, I was thinking of moving the spiritual weapon towards it or...

03:01:00.228 --> 03:01:06.468
Riswynn: But if it's gonna wake up before it can go 60 feet, then I'm just gonna wait for it to come to me, 'cause the thing's gonna run so fast.

03:01:06.468 --> 03:01:09.428
Delwath: It... Is there any signs that these things can

03:01:10.548 --> 03:01:12.628
Delwath: talk or communicate in any fashion?

03:01:14.888 --> 03:01:15.788
DM: I mean, they have

03:01:18.108 --> 03:01:22.688
DM: mouths. They seem to have some degree of intelligence.

03:01:22.688 --> 03:01:22.968
DM: Um,

03:01:24.568 --> 03:01:26.908
DM: they weren't necessarily talking to each other.

03:01:30.488 --> 03:01:34.508
DM: They're definitely not, you know, the brightest thing in the pa- in the

03:01:35.828 --> 03:01:37.068
DM: world.

03:01:37.068 --> 03:01:41.168
Wellby: Do we have any way to, like, tie it up while it's still asleep?

03:01:41.168 --> 03:01:44.028
Delwath: Yeah, I was just gonna s- I mean, I have some rope.

03:01:44.028 --> 03:01:45.748
DM: Yeah, you could tie it up with rope.

03:01:45.748 --> 03:01:48.668
DM: I'm... I think in 30 seconds if you run over there right away-

03:01:48.668 --> 03:01:48.758
Unknown: Yeah

03:01:48.758 --> 03:01:48.938
DM: ... you could,

03:01:50.088 --> 03:01:51.307
DM: you could get it tied up.

03:01:53.248 --> 03:01:53.268
Unknown: Yeah.

03:01:53.268 --> 03:01:55.028
Delwath: Cool. Delwath will go tie it up.

03:01:56.208 --> 03:01:56.508
Wellby: Yeah.

03:01:56.508 --> 03:01:57.588
DM: Okay, so, um-

03:01:57.588 --> 03:01:58.248
Wellby: Wellby will come help

03:01:58.248 --> 03:02:02.208
DM: ... so as you're tying it up, um, uh,

03:02:04.488 --> 03:02:08.428
DM: it's, it's, like, starting to wake up, and, um, you get it,

03:02:09.688 --> 03:02:15.448
DM: uh, you get it, like, well tied up, um, with, with rope, um,

03:02:17.868 --> 03:02:18.928
DM: not a garden hose.

03:02:20.208 --> 03:02:23.098
DM: [laughs] Um.

03:02:23.098 --> 03:02:23.108
Unknown: [laughs]

03:02:23.108 --> 03:02:25.668
DM: Cyberpunk reference. And, um,

03:02:26.908 --> 03:02:37.608
DM: as it starts to come to and just, uh, is, like, just kind of yelping and snarling at you and, you know, try- testing the ropes and,

03:02:37.608 --> 03:02:43.028
DM: and sort of trying to, to break through any kind of way it can, um,

03:02:45.088 --> 03:02:49.708
DM: just seems, like, horribly, like, angry and just

03:02:51.288 --> 03:02:52.348
DM: snarling mad.

03:02:53.448 --> 03:02:53.658
Unknown: Does it-

03:02:53.658 --> 03:02:55.948
DM: Doesn't seem to be speaking any particular language.

03:02:55.948 --> 03:02:59.868
DM: It doesn't turn to you and say, "Hey, let me go," or anything.

03:02:59.868 --> 03:03:00.468
DM: It's just...

03:03:01.988 --> 03:03:09.328
DM: It could be speaking some language if the language mostly consisted of, like, sort of growls and

03:03:10.388 --> 03:03:17.558
DM: yips and snarls and, you know, bits of- Uh, you know, guttural

03:03:18.978 --> 03:03:20.498
DM: cries and things like that.

03:03:22.158 --> 03:03:24.618
DM: Um- Not anything you recognize.

03:03:24.618 --> 03:03:24.918
DM: Right.

03:03:27.618 --> 03:03:29.708
Seeker: I wonder, though, I do have

03:03:31.178 --> 03:03:32.138
DM: speak with animals.

03:03:33.698 --> 03:03:35.098
DM: Hmm.

03:03:35.098 --> 03:03:37.558
DM: Uh, it is not actually an animal.

03:03:37.558 --> 03:03:39.638
Seeker: Oh, so it wouldn't, this wouldn't apply.

03:03:39.638 --> 03:03:40.658
DM: That would not apply.

03:03:44.238 --> 03:03:47.658
Kenzo: Um, are you guys all over there with the hyena thing?

03:03:47.658 --> 03:03:49.798
Delwath: Somebody should look at Ander.

03:03:49.798 --> 03:03:50.458
Wellby: Ander.

03:03:50.458 --> 03:03:52.118
DM: Worry about Ander.

03:03:52.118 --> 03:03:53.518
Wellby: Tim, do you see my message in chat?

03:03:54.638 --> 03:03:56.258
DM: Oh, uh...

03:03:59.678 --> 03:04:01.018
DM: Uh, he's... Okay, yeah.

03:04:02.958 --> 03:04:03.678
DM: Hold on one sec.

03:04:05.438 --> 03:04:07.898
Kenzo: So while you are all...

03:04:07.898 --> 03:04:08.278
Kenzo: Okay, so

03:04:09.938 --> 03:04:13.938
Kenzo: I guess, uh, Seeker, are you also with, with the hyena creature?

03:04:13.938 --> 03:04:16.858
Seeker: I was walking over to see if I could understand what it was saying.

03:04:16.858 --> 03:04:16.998
DM: Yeah.

03:04:18.008 --> 03:04:25.638
Kenzo: Okay. Um, as you all are kinda heading over there, um, Kenzo, you know, again, is like just, robes are just shredded.

03:04:25.638 --> 03:04:32.478
Kenzo: Um, somehow is, like, not dead, and basically, like, like, just isn't say- is, is not saying a word.

03:04:32.478 --> 03:04:36.868
Kenzo: Um, and then, like, basically kind of sits into a, um, [tsking]

03:04:38.078 --> 03:04:43.918
Kenzo: sort of a, a cross-legged, like, meditative pose, and is totally silent.

03:04:43.918 --> 03:04:47.218
Kenzo: But you all start feeling the earth shaking around him.

03:04:47.218 --> 03:04:47.778
Kenzo: It's like the earth-

03:04:47.778 --> 03:04:48.198
DM: Whoa

03:04:48.198 --> 03:04:50.538
Kenzo: ... is starting to, like, shake, like, all, all around him.

03:04:53.598 --> 03:04:55.778
Delwath: Around Kenzo or around?

03:04:55.778 --> 03:04:56.978
Kenzo: Around Kenzo. Yeah.

03:04:58.378 --> 03:04:58.598
DM: Whoa.

03:05:00.298 --> 03:05:05.858
Seeker: I, um, I turn back towards you, wondering how you caused a minor seismic event.

03:05:07.998 --> 03:05:13.418
Kenzo: It's not obvious. It's just, it's just, like, literally the earth around, around you, um, is, is shaking.

03:05:17.738 --> 03:05:19.258
DM: I send you a message, Schwartz.

03:05:19.258 --> 03:05:21.298
DM: [coughing]

03:05:23.238 --> 03:05:24.498
DM: So is anybody...

03:05:24.498 --> 03:05:27.498
DM: Did you actually go... Are you actually going over to him, Wellby?

03:05:29.398 --> 03:05:31.818
Wellby: No, I'm trying to talk to the hyena dude.

03:05:31.818 --> 03:05:33.138
DM: Oh, okay.

03:05:33.138 --> 03:05:34.978
DM: Is anybody going over to Ander?

03:05:36.928 --> 03:05:38.418
DM: He's starting to come around.

03:05:39.438 --> 03:05:41.118
DM: Somebody should, but-

03:05:41.118 --> 03:05:41.578
Riswynn: I'm not even sure-

03:05:41.578 --> 03:05:43.078
DM: Oh, oh, sorry. That's not...

03:05:43.078 --> 03:05:44.858
DM: Yeah, you don't get anything from the hyena dude.

03:05:44.858 --> 03:05:46.298
DM: I thought you were trying to talk to Ander.

03:05:48.658 --> 03:05:48.958
DM: Um,

03:05:51.658 --> 03:05:54.258
Seeker: uh, yeah, we should tie up Ander.

03:05:54.258 --> 03:05:55.318
DM: Um.

03:05:55.318 --> 03:05:57.148
Wellby: [laughs]

03:05:57.148 --> 03:05:57.738
DM: Also.

03:05:57.738 --> 03:05:58.678
Wellby: Uh, I'll, I'll go over to him.

03:05:58.678 --> 03:06:09.018
Riswynn: I wanted to keep an eye on Kenzo with a crazy guy like Ander in the vicinity, so I stayed where I was, but I didn't wanna approach the, the half, unknown halfling, 'cause I

03:06:09.018 --> 03:06:11.258
Riswynn: know he doesn't recognize me.

03:06:11.258 --> 03:06:13.068
Unknown: He's seen me before.

03:06:13.068 --> 03:06:14.358
Wellby: Yeah. Let's tie him up.

03:06:14.358 --> 03:06:16.338
Seeker: Yep. I'll, I'll help with that.

03:06:17.758 --> 03:06:19.658
DM: Okay, so as he... So the...

03:06:19.658 --> 03:06:25.438
DM: As he comes to, he also seems to be sort of, um, acting

03:06:27.098 --> 03:06:28.498
DM: similar to this other creature.

03:06:28.498 --> 03:06:34.978
DM: Like, he's sort of, um, snarling and angry and, you know, he's just, he's just sort of s-

03:06:36.118 --> 03:06:38.178
DM: screaming in frustration almost.

03:06:39.278 --> 03:06:39.858
DM: Hmm.

03:06:41.178 --> 03:06:42.938
Delwath: Does the hyena show, like...

03:06:46.227 --> 03:06:47.477
DM: Is, what's it carrying?

03:06:47.478 --> 03:06:49.218
Delwath: Does it have anything?

03:06:49.218 --> 03:06:50.477
DM: Two swords.

03:06:50.478 --> 03:06:51.958
DM: It has two swords.

03:06:51.958 --> 03:06:54.028
DM: Um, it has, um...

03:06:54.028 --> 03:06:55.138
DM: It's, you know, it's wearing

03:06:56.358 --> 03:06:59.538
DM: armor. It's not in, it's not, you know, good quality.

03:06:59.538 --> 03:07:01.158
DM: It's tattered.

03:07:01.158 --> 03:07:04.198
DM: Um, but it's, you know, um, like studded leather, right?

03:07:04.198 --> 03:07:10.998
DM: It's, it's, it's not carrying much else besides, uh, weapons and armor.

03:07:10.998 --> 03:07:14.198
DM: I mean, it has, you know, it has, um-

03:07:14.198 --> 03:07:14.838
DM: Food or water?

03:07:16.158 --> 03:07:19.298
DM: Uh, it does have wa- it does have a waterskin.

03:07:19.298 --> 03:07:28.318
DM: Um, there's a few strips of, like, um, raw flesh sort of tied around it, but it doesn't seem like it's carrying much in the way of food.

03:07:28.318 --> 03:07:28.538
DM: Um,

03:07:30.358 --> 03:07:34.378
DM: you know, it's, uh, it doesn't seem to have

03:07:35.458 --> 03:07:37.338
DM: a significant amount of gear.

03:07:37.338 --> 03:07:48.198
DM: There's a, you know, there's a, a leg of a goat tied or- tied in a loop slung over its back that's been partially gnawed on.

03:07:48.198 --> 03:07:51.778
DM: Um, and it has sort of a few bones, like,

03:07:52.878 --> 03:07:58.618
DM: sort of like a crudely constructed necklace type thing, like, tied as, like, an amulet or something around its neck.

03:07:59.818 --> 03:08:02.118
Unknown: What are the bones of?

03:08:04.238 --> 03:08:07.058
DM: They're, like, knucklebones of probably not a...

03:08:07.058 --> 03:08:08.178
DM: Well, make a medicine check.

03:08:11.278 --> 03:08:13.398
Delwath: And these, we're on the north side of town, right?

03:08:13.398 --> 03:08:15.478
Delwath: These guys were coming from the north? Um, yes.

03:08:15.478 --> 03:08:16.678
DM: Coming from the north. Um,

03:08:17.918 --> 03:08:22.778
DM: it's, I mean, they're, like, mammalian, uh, like, uh,

03:08:25.818 --> 03:08:34.018
DM: uh, probably bones from some sort of, um, like, antelope or ungulate or some sort of animal like that.

03:08:34.018 --> 03:08:38.717
DM: Like, bits of the ankle, bits of the, of the wrist bone.

03:08:38.718 --> 03:08:41.678
DM: Like, just little bone fragments from something like that.

03:08:41.678 --> 03:08:44.298
DM: Doesn't seem to be humanoid, but you're not entirely sure.

03:08:45.598 --> 03:08:45.838
DM: Oof.

03:08:49.578 --> 03:08:49.908
DM: And

03:08:51.618 --> 03:08:55.758
Seeker: in terms of the body structure, like, which parts are human?

03:08:55.758 --> 03:08:57.518
Seeker: Which parts are hyena?

03:08:57.518 --> 03:09:06.478
DM: It's basically a, like, a humanoid, hands and le- uh, hands normal like a, like a humanoid.

03:09:06.478 --> 03:09:10.998
DM: Um, but it clearly can ru- you saw it running on all four.

03:09:10.998 --> 03:09:22.442
DM: Its back legs are much more hyena-like, and then it has basically a hyena-like face and sort of mane stretching back down its neck, and big ears.

03:09:22.442 --> 03:09:26.382
DM: And like teeth, like very, you know, carnivore scavenger teeth.

03:09:28.942 --> 03:09:34.122
DM: So it's really sort of its torso and arms that are the most humanoid-like.

03:09:38.042 --> 03:09:40.222
Seeker: Freaky. Turn some

03:09:42.122 --> 03:09:43.462
Seeker: music up.

03:09:47.422 --> 03:09:47.962
Seeker: And, uh,

03:09:49.002 --> 03:09:49.422
Seeker: Ander

03:09:51.022 --> 03:09:51.842
Seeker: and the hyena thing

03:09:53.142 --> 03:09:55.022
Seeker: had a similar affect.

03:09:55.022 --> 03:09:57.722
Seeker: [sniffs] This was sort of like incoherent bloodlust.

03:09:58.782 --> 03:10:03.322
DM: Um, yeah, so I mean, just, it's more sort of anger.

03:10:03.322 --> 03:10:09.962
DM: You, you... It's like, I mean, Ander is sort of yelling almost like, uh, in disappointment and anger.

03:10:11.782 --> 03:10:12.802
DM: He's just kind of-

03:10:12.802 --> 03:10:17.182
Riswynn: Was it more responding towards the maws originally, and now that they're gone, he's chilling out?

03:10:17.182 --> 03:10:20.702
Riswynn: Or is he, like, now sort of focused on the hyena somehow?

03:10:20.702 --> 03:10:25.362
DM: He doesn't seem... He, yeah, he was definitely running towards the mouth creatures.

03:10:27.142 --> 03:10:29.322
Seeker: Why? That's weird.

03:10:29.322 --> 03:10:39.402
Wellby: He... I'll, I'll say to everyone, he was saying that he was ready to be eaten, that he wanted to be eaten, as if he was running to them in order to be consumed

03:10:39.402 --> 03:10:40.122
Wellby: by them.

03:10:41.522 --> 03:10:44.502
Seeker: Has anybody seen anything like these mouths on legs before?

03:10:46.762 --> 03:10:46.902
Seeker: [sniffs]

03:10:46.902 --> 03:10:49.682
DM: Uh, make an arcana check, Seeker.

03:10:51.682 --> 03:10:52.162
Seeker: Do-do-

03:10:52.162 --> 03:10:54.302
DM: And, Delwath, you're proficient in arcana, right?

03:10:54.302 --> 03:10:54.482
Seeker: Yep.

03:10:56.632 --> 03:10:58.982
Seeker: Uh. Eight.

03:10:58.982 --> 03:10:59.422
DM: Uh,

03:11:06.702 --> 03:11:07.182
DM: so

03:11:08.542 --> 03:11:09.862
DM: let's see. Um.

03:11:12.322 --> 03:11:14.012
Seeker: I read a whole book about mouth creatures.

03:11:16.102 --> 03:11:17.512
DM: [laughs]

03:11:17.512 --> 03:11:19.522
Wellby: [laughs] They're the natural enemy of dentists.

03:11:19.522 --> 03:11:21.102
Seeker: [laughs]

03:11:21.102 --> 03:11:22.682
Kenzo: Just part of your undergrad thesis, I thought.

03:11:23.942 --> 03:11:25.042
Seeker: Exactly. [laughs]

03:11:25.042 --> 03:11:27.642
Wellby: Mouth creatures are an essential part of geology.

03:11:27.642 --> 03:11:29.302
DM: So, so-

03:11:29.302 --> 03:11:29.622
Wellby: [laughs]

03:11:29.622 --> 03:11:31.402
DM: [laughs] Yeah. Yeah.

03:11:31.402 --> 03:11:33.602
DM: They're an essential part of geology.

03:11:33.602 --> 03:11:33.802
DM: You,

03:11:35.282 --> 03:11:35.422
DM: uh,

03:11:36.622 --> 03:11:42.081
DM: so you, you think about this for a while and, um, you recall, uh...

03:11:42.082 --> 03:11:48.342
DM: Right, so you are, you've been interested in sort of the idea of other planes and how that connects to magic for a long time.

03:11:48.342 --> 03:11:58.082
DM: And so at one point, you studied, uh, back, you know, before you even left your home city in one of the older libraries there.

03:11:58.082 --> 03:12:06.322
DM: And, um, there was a book on, um, in, called Intrusions From the Darker Planes.

03:12:07.902 --> 03:12:08.422
DM: And,

03:12:09.782 --> 03:12:16.582
DM: uh, in that book, a lot of it was sort of speculation about, you know, the kinds of creatures and, and,

03:12:17.642 --> 03:12:18.362
DM: uh, sort of

03:12:19.922 --> 03:12:26.092
DM: evil that can seep through the, the darker places in the multiverse.

03:12:26.092 --> 03:12:30.442
DM: And you remember seeing a picture that looked very similar to this, um,

03:12:31.482 --> 03:12:31.622
DM: uh,

03:12:32.862 --> 03:12:35.222
DM: described as being, um,

03:12:37.962 --> 03:12:44.662
DM: the sort of foot soldiers in the army of the, um, dark lord of hunger.

03:12:47.142 --> 03:12:48.712
Seeker: Appropriate.

03:12:48.712 --> 03:12:48.742
Wellby: Hmm.

03:12:48.742 --> 03:12:51.422
Seeker: I'm gonna relay this information, as strange as it sounds.

03:12:52.782 --> 03:12:53.142
Wellby: Hmm.

03:12:53.142 --> 03:13:03.392
DM: And it seemed clear from that book that these were extra planar entities, like they were not from this world, was the description, was the context

03:13:03.392 --> 03:13:05.402
DM: that you would have read this in.

03:13:05.402 --> 03:13:06.702
Seeker: But how would they get here?

03:13:09.942 --> 03:13:10.382
Seeker: Man.

03:13:12.762 --> 03:13:16.282
DM: So you do know that there are, you know, there are some

03:13:17.822 --> 03:13:23.562
DM: more powerful magics that can summon demons and other creatures like that.

03:13:23.562 --> 03:13:23.582
DM: Um,

03:13:24.922 --> 03:13:26.202
DM: so it's definitely possible.

03:13:26.202 --> 03:13:29.082
DM: It's something you've aware is, uh,

03:13:31.002 --> 03:13:35.142
DM: not out of the realm of possibility, but it requires fairly powerful magics to do.

03:13:46.782 --> 03:13:47.122
Seeker: Uh,

03:13:48.422 --> 03:13:52.842
Seeker: we should try to regroup and, and make sure nothing else comes in.

03:13:52.842 --> 03:13:54.482
Riswynn: We kill the hyena thing?

03:13:54.482 --> 03:13:56.302
Riswynn: Not really telling us anything.

03:13:56.302 --> 03:13:57.362
Riswynn: We don't want it to get loose.

03:13:58.642 --> 03:13:59.882
Seeker: Oh, yeah. What do you do with the hyena thing?

03:14:03.362 --> 03:14:06.062
Delwath: I mean, does it seem...

03:14:06.062 --> 03:14:09.602
Delwath: It, it doesn't respond to attempts to communicate with it.

03:14:09.602 --> 03:14:10.262
Riswynn: Right.

03:14:10.262 --> 03:14:10.272
DM: No.

03:14:10.272 --> 03:14:13.342
Riswynn: So if we, like, let it free, it's not just gonna run away.

03:14:14.752 --> 03:14:14.782
Riswynn: [laughs]

03:14:14.782 --> 03:14:16.142
Seeker: There's no rehabilitation.

03:14:19.902 --> 03:14:22.742
Wellby: Yeah, the, it's, it's all retributive justice.

03:14:22.742 --> 03:14:23.442
Seeker: [laughs]

03:14:24.862 --> 03:14:25.602
Seeker: Retributive.

03:14:25.602 --> 03:14:29.102
Wellby: There's no sense of restorative justice in Kalgura.

03:14:30.122 --> 03:14:31.662
Seeker: [laughs] Brutal.

03:14:33.502 --> 03:14:36.042
Delwath: So I think there's no way that it, I mean,

03:14:37.622 --> 03:14:38.882
DM: yeah, it doesn't...

03:14:38.882 --> 03:14:43.702
Delwath: I was more thinking there's no way we could, you know, it wouldn't lead us back to its base or anything like that.

03:14:43.702 --> 03:14:44.812
DM: It seems too far,

03:14:46.382 --> 03:14:50.122
DM: uh- You get the sense that if you untie it, it's just gonna attack you.

03:14:50.122 --> 03:14:51.542
Seeker: Attack, yeah, that's, yeah.

03:14:51.542 --> 03:14:54.882
DM: Keep trying to attack you until you or it are dead.

03:14:54.882 --> 03:15:00.082
Wellby: Can we tell anything, like, looking at that and the other dead creatures, anything about where they might have come from?

03:15:00.082 --> 03:15:02.582
Wellby: You know, the difference between, like, the-

03:15:02.582 --> 03:15:03.582
DM: I mean, let's kill it

03:15:03.582 --> 03:15:08.182
Wellby: ... sandy desert to the south versus, like, the, I don't know, the-

03:15:08.182 --> 03:15:14.442
DM: So they, it, they, at least just from looking around, they probably came from the north.

03:15:14.442 --> 03:15:14.682
Wellby: Oh.

03:15:14.682 --> 03:15:16.022
Seeker: Can we follow their tracks?

03:15:16.022 --> 03:15:17.002
Seeker: We did a good job on the last ones.

03:15:17.002 --> 03:15:18.722
Wellby: Yes, we can.

03:15:18.722 --> 03:15:21.462
DM: You can. [laughs] Indeed, you can.

03:15:22.542 --> 03:15:26.842
Seeker: We should um see if the mouth creatures make distinct tracks and if they came from the same place or-

03:15:26.842 --> 03:15:28.902
Delwath: So let's kill this hyena thing.

03:15:28.902 --> 03:15:34.682
Delwath: Let some, somebody go or all of us go maybe reassure the town that they didn't, you know, that...

03:15:37.852 --> 03:15:39.321
DM: They should flee probably.

03:15:39.322 --> 03:15:40.822
Delwath: Advance your fleeing timetable.

03:15:42.342 --> 03:15:42.942
Seeker: Right.

03:15:42.942 --> 03:15:43.702
Wellby: To now.

03:15:45.022 --> 03:15:47.982
Wellby: I'll, I'll take, uh, Ander back to the halfling as well.

03:15:47.982 --> 03:15:58.782
DM: Okay, so as you, as you start to take him back, um, uh, Bri and Callie you see sort of running from the distance, and as they see you with him and him walking,

03:15:58.782 --> 03:16:08.802
DM: um, and he seems, at this stage he seems ki- almost catatonic, like he's, uh, you know, very much entered the kind of, uh, depressive phase of

03:16:08.802 --> 03:16:18.512
DM: his, his cycle, and um, is just kind of whimpering to himself and occasionally, like, complaining of being hungry and

03:16:19.542 --> 03:16:20.942
DM: moving slowly.

03:16:20.942 --> 03:16:21.382
DM: And they're,

03:16:23.242 --> 03:16:23.422
DM: um,

03:16:24.802 --> 03:16:29.582
DM: they're quite, uh, relieved, extremely relieved to see him alive.

03:16:29.582 --> 03:16:34.562
DM: Um, and Callie just kind of looks shocked at you, and, "He just,

03:16:36.042 --> 03:16:37.402
DM: he just ran off. We w- we

03:16:38.762 --> 03:16:40.242
DM: heard these things coming and we

03:16:41.502 --> 03:16:44.262
DM: ran with everybody else as far as we could, and he just,

03:16:46.142 --> 03:16:48.342
DM: he just turned and ran

03:16:50.142 --> 03:16:51.562
DM: straight towards them."

03:16:54.602 --> 03:17:00.142
Wellby: So he was trying to feed himself to one of those, looking at the moths.

03:17:00.142 --> 03:17:00.522
DM: She like,

03:17:01.662 --> 03:17:11.202
DM: uh, just like her face turns white and she like steps back in horror and says, just like holds her arm up, "No, don't...

03:17:12.262 --> 03:17:12.762
DM: I can't."

03:17:13.802 --> 03:17:17.202
DM: And she like turns her back and is, "Don't tell me what that was.

03:17:17.202 --> 03:17:17.302
DM: I...

03:17:18.882 --> 03:17:20.702
DM: It's already gonna live in my nightmares.

03:17:20.702 --> 03:17:23.822
DM: I do not want to see any, know anything more about this.

03:17:23.822 --> 03:17:23.832
DM: I,

03:17:26.442 --> 03:17:28.002
DM: I hope you can do something for him.

03:17:28.002 --> 03:17:29.302
DM: I hope you can find some,

03:17:31.182 --> 03:17:31.941
DM: some clue."

03:17:34.722 --> 03:17:37.221
DM: And she's like, there's like tears kind of coming down her face.

03:17:37.222 --> 03:17:37.522
DM: She's

03:17:39.942 --> 03:17:45.002
DM: clearly extremely distraught at this news and the sight of this battle.

03:17:47.162 --> 03:17:47.402
Wellby: Wellby-

03:17:47.402 --> 03:17:47.682
DM: And then-

03:17:47.682 --> 03:17:52.202
Wellby: ... attempts to be comforting, but W- Wellby is very much like not a people person.

03:17:52.202 --> 03:17:52.502
Wellby: He's like very-

03:17:52.502 --> 03:17:52.942
DM: [laughs]

03:17:52.942 --> 03:17:55.362
Wellby: ... very bad people skills.

03:17:55.362 --> 03:18:01.962
Wellby: He's like, "Well, we'll, we'll track them back north and attempt either to break the spell or,

03:18:03.122 --> 03:18:05.022
Unknown: or let you know we have them."

03:18:06.172 --> 03:18:16.342
DM: They, so they, they, halflings kind of shuffle off as you hear, um, uh, hoof beats coming from the east as, um, Havdar rides

03:18:16.342 --> 03:18:16.922
DM: up, um,

03:18:18.402 --> 03:18:24.302
DM: his spear bloodied and like a gash across his chest, and he says, "Ooh, thank God.

03:18:26.572 --> 03:18:33.682
DM: I saw the dostan was running in this direction, um, when two of these..."

03:18:33.682 --> 03:18:34.642
DM: And he looks around

03:18:35.882 --> 03:18:39.842
DM: at the bodies, and he sees these like hyena creatures.

03:18:39.842 --> 03:18:44.962
DM: Um, "Two of these attacked, uh, on the other side of the hill,

03:18:46.922 --> 03:18:48.582
DM: and I, they seemed like they were

03:18:51.022 --> 03:18:51.562
DM: sneaky.

03:18:53.742 --> 03:19:03.862
DM: They were shooting at people with arrows, and I charged towards them just praying that as I saw the four of you run off, five of you run off, you would be able

03:19:03.862 --> 03:19:05.802
DM: to deal with these attackers.

03:19:05.802 --> 03:19:05.982
DM: Um,

03:19:07.942 --> 03:19:10.002
DM: I think we have to leave first thing in the morning.

03:19:14.062 --> 03:19:20.162
DM: These are the same sorts of creatures that were attacking Bas Udda, and if they're coming from the north now as well,

03:19:23.882 --> 03:19:25.622
DM: we have to leave as quickly as we can."

03:19:28.282 --> 03:19:32.721
Kenzo: So by the way, this whole time, everything that's been going on, Kenzo has not moved.

03:19:32.722 --> 03:19:35.342
Kenzo: Kenzo has just like stayed exactly...

03:19:35.342 --> 03:19:42.282
Kenzo: The earth was shaking for a little while, and he's just not moved, stayed in meditative pose this entire time, just like not, just, just sitting there.

03:19:44.962 --> 03:19:46.412
Seeker: Mm.

03:19:48.382 --> 03:19:49.282
Wellby: You do this often?

03:19:50.702 --> 03:19:51.902
Wellby: Have you all seen this before?

03:19:54.122 --> 03:19:56.992
Seeker: Well, he is a monk, but we haven't seen this specific thing.

03:19:56.992 --> 03:19:57.322
Kenzo: No.

03:20:00.762 --> 03:20:01.682
Seeker: Wait, so h-

03:20:01.682 --> 03:20:03.132
Wellby: Check your, uh, messages.

03:20:05.382 --> 03:20:08.922
Seeker: Ha- Havdar's the guy that just rode up?

03:20:08.922 --> 03:20:10.182
DM: Yeah.

03:20:10.182 --> 03:20:10.482
Seeker: Um,

03:20:12.502 --> 03:20:20.722
Seeker: uh, we should let you know that in addition to these hy- hyena guys, we just defeated, uh, a s- a much stranger group of creatures.

03:20:20.722 --> 03:20:23.482
Seeker: They were all mouth, you might say.

03:20:23.482 --> 03:20:25.802
Seeker: I don't know if there's any identifiable remains

03:20:25.802 --> 03:20:26.342
Seeker: that I can point you to.

03:20:26.342 --> 03:20:32.502
DM: There's some bits. I mean, the one that Riswynn destroyed with the spell is pretty much scattered to pieces, but-

03:20:32.502 --> 03:20:33.562
Seeker: Nice

03:20:33.562 --> 03:20:34.002
Wellby: Sorry

03:20:34.002 --> 03:20:34.841
DM: ... um, the-

03:20:34.841 --> 03:20:36.692
Seeker: [laughs]

03:20:36.692 --> 03:20:43.462
DM: ... the war hammer, uh, the, the other two are still like intact enough you can look at their corpses.

03:20:43.462 --> 03:20:43.702
Seeker: Right.

03:20:43.702 --> 03:20:51.142
DM: Um, and as you, as you, uh, are sort of standing here, you can see that the corpses are like decaying

03:20:52.722 --> 03:20:54.102
DM: faster than normal, right?

03:20:54.102 --> 03:21:01.902
DM: Like, they're already starting to rot a little bit, and like the rot is kind of seeping into the ground slightly around them, um,

03:21:03.942 --> 03:21:10.262
DM: almost like bruised f- like they're just, like their flesh is all becoming bruised and, and beaten as they

03:21:11.662 --> 03:21:14.962
DM: start to decay and fade away.

03:21:14.962 --> 03:21:17.682
DM: Like, and they're fading away instead of decaying, right?

03:21:17.682 --> 03:21:21.582
DM: Like, the one that's, is shattered into pieces is just gone.

03:21:21.582 --> 03:21:24.901
DM: There's not little bits of flesh scattered around the battlefield.

03:21:24.902 --> 03:21:26.542
DM: It's just gone.

03:21:29.894 --> 03:21:30.754
Seeker: How does Havdar react?

03:21:30.754 --> 03:21:32.634
DM: Well, he, uh...

03:21:32.634 --> 03:21:40.074
DM: I mean, you can see he wasn't expecting that, and he sort of steels himself a little bit and tries, you know, is acting.

03:21:40.074 --> 03:21:41.234
DM: You know, he is like a, you know,

03:21:42.394 --> 03:21:43.754
DM: Aradin warrior dude.

03:21:43.754 --> 03:21:49.394
DM: He's not gonna let himself show fear or confusion in front of you.

03:21:49.394 --> 03:21:51.894
DM: But he, you know, you can...

03:21:51.894 --> 03:21:55.164
DM: He takes, takes a step back on his horse, and you can tell that wasn't,

03:21:56.514 --> 03:21:57.424
DM: that wasn't his

03:21:58.554 --> 03:22:01.554
DM: expectation. He thought you were fighting more of these, uh-

03:22:03.254 --> 03:22:03.954
Seeker: Hyena

03:22:03.954 --> 03:22:05.444
DM: ... hyena, hyena creatures.

03:22:07.794 --> 03:22:10.074
DM: "That is, uh, unsettling.

03:22:11.414 --> 03:22:15.854
DM: I am impressed with your prowess in not, uh,

03:22:16.974 --> 03:22:22.054
DM: blanching in the face of a creature with so many teeth.

03:22:22.054 --> 03:22:24.914
DM: But I have not seen such a thing before."

03:22:24.914 --> 03:22:26.234
Seeker: They seem to be very dangerous.

03:22:27.584 --> 03:22:28.194
DM: "Perhaps

03:22:30.254 --> 03:22:31.734
DM: came from the Blasted Plains.

03:22:31.734 --> 03:22:32.253
DM: There is...

03:22:33.894 --> 03:22:35.454
DM: could be anything out there."

03:22:39.014 --> 03:22:39.504
Seeker: From my-

03:22:39.504 --> 03:22:42.874
DM: Or do you think it came from the north, from Raven's Hold?

03:22:42.874 --> 03:22:43.054
Seeker: From my-

03:22:43.054 --> 03:22:45.264
DM: I guess there could be anything there, either

03:22:45.264 --> 03:22:52.654
Seeker: ... from my studies, as far as I know, this type of creature comes not from this world at all, but from another,

03:22:53.934 --> 03:22:54.874
Seeker: from a darker plane.

03:22:56.114 --> 03:22:57.634
Seeker: Who knows how they got here.

03:22:57.634 --> 03:22:58.674
Seeker: We'd like to try to find out.

03:23:02.374 --> 03:23:03.114
DM: That is a...

03:23:04.994 --> 03:23:07.034
DM: Sounds like a dangerous mission, but...

03:23:08.254 --> 03:23:10.344
DM: And now he's, like, looking around, and he's like, uh,

03:23:11.574 --> 03:23:16.834
DM: turns to Riswynn and says, "I don't believe we've been introduced."

03:23:16.834 --> 03:23:19.214
DM: Sort of gives a little bow. Havdar.

03:23:20.034 --> 03:23:20.554
Riswynn: Riswynn.

03:23:21.734 --> 03:23:22.934
DM: Are you with them?

03:23:24.694 --> 03:23:31.834
Riswynn: It seemed prudent with such things about to, uh, join some other travelers headed in the same direction, so, uh-

03:23:31.834 --> 03:23:33.754
DM: You're heading to Raven's Hold.

03:23:33.754 --> 03:23:34.114
Riswynn: I am.

03:23:37.134 --> 03:23:38.653
DM: I wish you luck.

03:23:38.654 --> 03:23:42.354
DM: I must return and, uh, supervise the

03:23:43.874 --> 03:23:45.134
DM: gathering of forces.

03:23:45.134 --> 03:23:51.394
DM: I, I suspect that we will be packing and preparing all night, but I am...

03:23:51.394 --> 03:23:55.154
DM: I will tell Kendros and Kisa that we must leave at first light.

03:23:56.494 --> 03:23:58.093
DM: The village is clearly not safe.

03:24:00.754 --> 03:24:03.714
DM: I would advise you do the same as well and find out all you can.

03:24:08.574 --> 03:24:14.974
Riswynn: The hyena creatures you encountered, you were able to, to take them both down, or did they head off in some direction?

03:24:14.974 --> 03:24:18.114
DM: Oh, yes, I, I, I was able to take them down.

03:24:18.114 --> 03:24:26.014
DM: Uh, nasty barbed arrows, but nothing that a few quick spear thrusts and a horse charge can't cure.

03:24:26.014 --> 03:24:27.934
Seeker: One of, one of ours we put magically to sleep.

03:24:27.934 --> 03:24:29.974
Seeker: What's its status now?

03:24:29.974 --> 03:24:31.544
Unknown: We, we killed it.

03:24:31.544 --> 03:24:32.664
DM: They killed it.

03:24:32.664 --> 03:24:33.094
Seeker: Oh. Never mind.

03:24:35.734 --> 03:24:36.494
Riswynn: Ours had swords,

03:24:37.674 --> 03:24:39.674
Riswynn: but we'll keep an eye out for the barbed arrows.

03:24:41.214 --> 03:24:42.214
Seeker: That sounds nasty, too.

03:24:44.054 --> 03:24:44.093
Seeker: Um-

03:24:44.094 --> 03:24:45.714
DM: Well, watch your backs.

03:24:45.714 --> 03:24:48.464
DM: Travel quick, travel quiet, travel carefully.

03:24:50.034 --> 03:24:50.474
DM: I will

03:24:53.014 --> 03:24:57.074
DM: hope to see you in some time when I can return with f- in force

03:24:58.354 --> 03:25:01.294
DM: to launch our attack once we know more as to what we're fighting.

03:25:01.294 --> 03:25:01.554
DM: But

03:25:03.014 --> 03:25:04.714
DM: I think given this news, I am,

03:25:06.074 --> 03:25:08.754
DM: I am glad we did not go charging off to the south.

03:25:08.754 --> 03:25:09.914
DM: If there were more of these

03:25:12.054 --> 03:25:17.894
DM: dark creatures from another plane, as you say, I'm not sure that would have been a prudent course of action.

03:25:20.754 --> 03:25:25.914
Seeker: We'll just hope those staying here to protect the temple to Shakun have sufficient defenses.

03:25:29.074 --> 03:25:31.554
DM: I will say I think you've done a nice job.

03:25:31.554 --> 03:25:33.654
DM: I was inspecting it this morning.

03:25:33.654 --> 03:25:34.054
Seeker: Oh, thanks.

03:25:35.114 --> 03:25:43.354
DM: The fortifications are, I think, the best we could do in the time, and I will pray for their safety.

03:25:43.354 --> 03:25:46.253
DM: I'm sure they will pray for their safety as well.

03:25:48.274 --> 03:25:50.574
DM: With that, I must away.

03:25:50.574 --> 03:25:56.934
DM: And he rides off, and there's, you know, as he rides into town, you can tell there's sort of commotion in the distance.

03:25:56.934 --> 03:25:58.514
DM: And, um,

03:26:00.274 --> 03:26:02.034
DM: you know, people are

03:26:03.454 --> 03:26:13.574
DM: shifting quickly from what normally would have been a sort of celebratory feast at the end of the festival as the Shrine of Jeevali's grows,

03:26:13.574 --> 03:26:15.224
DM: um, into its, into its

03:26:16.454 --> 03:26:17.464
DM: f- uh, sort of fused,

03:26:18.514 --> 03:26:23.484
DM: uh, divinely imbued form, to a hurried evacuation,

03:26:24.654 --> 03:26:26.814
DM: gathering in the night what they can.

03:26:26.814 --> 03:26:26.994
DM: Um,

03:26:28.654 --> 03:26:28.854
DM: you know,

03:26:30.214 --> 03:26:34.534
DM: horse-- getting on horses and just moving as fast as they can.

03:26:34.534 --> 03:26:39.604
DM: Many of the people who are here are, you know, came in for the festival and so are,

03:26:40.714 --> 03:26:42.954
DM: uh, prepared to travel.

03:26:42.954 --> 03:26:43.314
DM: Um,

03:26:45.254 --> 03:26:46.184
DM: many are,

03:26:47.474 --> 03:26:49.034
DM: you know, leaving their homes.

03:26:49.034 --> 03:26:52.114
DM: But given what's happened this evening, it's...

03:26:52.114 --> 03:26:54.754
DM: Everybody is in a state of just

03:26:55.874 --> 03:26:56.474
DM: flat-out

03:26:58.574 --> 03:26:59.774
DM: preparation to flee.

03:27:02.194 --> 03:27:02.474
DM: Um,

03:27:03.914 --> 03:27:11.624
DM: you know, Kisa and Kendrosa come to thank you and wish you off and, um, say, you know, "This,

03:27:13.234 --> 03:27:14.554
DM: this does not change our plans.

03:27:14.554 --> 03:27:16.784
DM: It just advances the timeline, and-"

03:27:18.034 --> 03:27:19.414
Kenzo: Sorry, have we gone into town?

03:27:19.414 --> 03:27:21.774
Kenzo: Because Kenzo's not moved. Kenzo's just, like, is still-

03:27:21.774 --> 03:27:23.354
DM: No, people are coming out here

03:27:23.354 --> 03:27:25.034
Kenzo: ... 00:06:05. Okay, okay.

03:27:25.034 --> 03:27:25.194
DM: Um,

03:27:26.894 --> 03:27:29.654
DM: the, you know, "This changes nothing.

03:27:29.654 --> 03:27:35.450
DM: This-" Just means we must flee as quickly as we can.

03:27:37.870 --> 03:27:47.990
DM: And Candrosa and the other, um, Mistai who are staying are, like, loading barrels of water up through this r- this, uh, rope pulling system through the second

03:27:47.990 --> 03:27:58.170
DM: story window and, you know, bringing in all the food that's left in town, and basically preparing to lock themselves in the temple and, you know, remain

03:27:58.170 --> 03:28:02.550
DM: boarded up as much as they can until you return.

03:28:04.350 --> 03:28:05.790
DM: And with that, um,

03:28:06.930 --> 03:28:08.170
DM: you rest.

03:28:08.170 --> 03:28:11.030
DM: Are you gonna stay, Kenzo, just meditating out here through the night?

03:28:12.310 --> 03:28:15.220
Kenzo: Um, is anybody co- gonna come and say anything to me or just, you're just, like, ignoring me?

03:28:15.220 --> 03:28:17.320
DM: Well, yeah, [laughs] that's a good question. Is anybody gonna say anything to you?

03:28:17.320 --> 03:28:23.210
Kenzo: Well, I, as a thought, like, Havdar, I don't know if you would've noticed, like, I was just, like, kinda sitting there or f- like, if they were gonna come, and I- I just have not moved.

03:28:23.210 --> 03:28:23.690
Kenzo: I'm like, I'm gonna-

03:28:23.690 --> 03:28:29.170
DM: So that's why Ken- I mean, Candrosa, when Candrosa comes up, he does, uh, sort of

03:28:30.770 --> 03:28:32.880
DM: look over at you. Is Kenzo okay?

03:28:35.030 --> 03:28:37.670
Seeker: He was badly injured in the fighting.

03:28:38.710 --> 03:28:40.910
Kenzo: Just so y- so you're actually asking if I'm okay?

03:28:40.910 --> 03:28:44.610
Kenzo: Is anybody talking to me or is anybody j- is everybody just talking about me after the-

03:28:44.610 --> 03:28:44.800
Seeker: I think after the-

03:28:44.800 --> 03:28:46.330
Seeker: I think we're just talking about you.

03:28:46.330 --> 03:28:55.570
Delwath: Well, I'll come up to Kenzo after the, like, after Havdar leaves and sit down sort of next to you and just ask,

03:28:57.270 --> 03:29:01.870
Delwath: and just look, like, look at Kenzo like, "Are you responding to somebody being near you?"

03:29:02.890 --> 03:29:09.990
Kenzo: So if you come over and, like, kinda sit down near me, then, then yeah, then Kenzo kinda stirs a little bit and then...

03:29:09.990 --> 03:29:11.010
Kenzo: So it's just y- it's just Delwath?

03:29:12.750 --> 03:29:13.750
Seeker: Yeah, I think so.

03:29:13.750 --> 03:29:23.790
Kenzo: Okay. So yeah, so Kenzo kind of, kind of, like, stirs a little bit and then, like, like, kind of, you know, comes out of his, his meditation, out of his trance, and he looks at you, but his eyes

03:29:23.790 --> 03:29:33.290
Kenzo: are, like, bright blue, like, just brilliant blue eyes, and he just kind of looks at you and then, um, uh, you know, he says, "Delwath,

03:29:35.710 --> 03:29:36.630
Kenzo: is the battle over?"

03:29:38.770 --> 03:29:39.090
Seeker: Yes.

03:29:41.470 --> 03:29:41.930
Kenzo: Did we win?

03:29:43.630 --> 03:29:44.430
Seeker: Yes, you were there.

03:29:47.350 --> 03:29:47.590
Kenzo: Right.

03:29:48.690 --> 03:29:55.410
Seeker: So I've, I've been, um, rummaging around in the ruins, trying to extract one of the, um, teeth of the mouth creatures.

03:29:56.670 --> 03:29:56.870
Seeker: Uh-

03:29:56.870 --> 03:29:58.030
DM: Okay

03:29:58.030 --> 03:30:01.950
Seeker: ... but, um, I, I, I turn when I, when I hear the voices,

03:30:04.770 --> 03:30:08.570
Seeker: uh, and s- and see the glowing of the eyes and-

03:30:08.570 --> 03:30:10.650
Delwath: This is unusu- your eyes are not normally blue?

03:30:10.650 --> 03:30:12.610
Kenzo: Yeah, no, they're normally, like, brown eyes, so.

03:30:12.610 --> 03:30:12.950
DM: Yeah.

03:30:12.950 --> 03:30:20.369
Kenzo: They're like piercing, like, blue eyes, like, like diamonds, like, incredibly, like, bright blue eyes.

03:30:20.370 --> 03:30:22.790
Seeker: Now, when you sh- did your Hadouken, was that blue?

03:30:24.290 --> 03:30:25.730
Kenzo: Um, sure.

03:30:25.730 --> 03:30:27.350
Kenzo: Yeah. It w- it was.

03:30:27.350 --> 03:30:27.900
Seeker: Nice, okay.

03:30:27.900 --> 03:30:29.050
Wellby: It's the snow cone

03:30:29.050 --> 03:30:29.730
Kenzo: ... mm-hmm.

03:30:29.730 --> 03:30:33.690
Seeker: The j- [laughs] A glowing blue ball of force.

03:30:33.690 --> 03:30:34.860
Kenzo: Yeah, exactly.

03:30:34.860 --> 03:30:35.290
Seeker: Love it. That works.

03:30:35.290 --> 03:30:36.790
Kenzo: Totally blue. No, perfect. I love that.

03:30:36.790 --> 03:30:37.210
Kenzo: Yes.

03:30:37.210 --> 03:30:37.440
Seeker: Mm-hmm.

03:30:39.170 --> 03:30:39.630
Seeker: Um,

03:30:42.970 --> 03:30:45.970
Seeker: just kinda stare at your glowing eyes for a second.

03:30:48.930 --> 03:30:49.310
Kenzo: Um...

03:30:51.130 --> 03:30:53.510
Unknown: Say, "Hey, Kenzo, you good?"

03:30:55.550 --> 03:30:56.190
Kenzo: I don't know.

03:30:57.610 --> 03:30:58.870
Kenzo: I don't know.

03:30:58.870 --> 03:31:02.610
Kenzo: I feel like I've, I've, uh, crossed into the void.

03:31:05.190 --> 03:31:07.350
Seeker: You, you took a lot of bites from these guys.

03:31:07.350 --> 03:31:10.230
Seeker: I hold up the... Did I find a tooth, Tim?

03:31:10.230 --> 03:31:10.670
DM: Uh, yeah.

03:31:11.810 --> 03:31:12.810
DM: You can extract a tooth.

03:31:12.810 --> 03:31:12.850
Seeker: Do you think-

03:31:12.850 --> 03:31:19.490
DM: I mean, it's, it's, it's black and it's a, it's almost steaming and it feels slightly warm to the touch.

03:31:19.490 --> 03:31:19.580
Seeker: Okay.

03:31:19.580 --> 03:31:21.050
DM: But you can extract one.

03:31:22.770 --> 03:31:23.320
Seeker: Uh, yeah.

03:31:23.320 --> 03:31:28.750
Riswynn: I throw a waterskin towards Kenzo if he needs some more physical recoveries.

03:31:28.750 --> 03:31:28.970
Seeker: Nice.

03:31:30.030 --> 03:31:31.590
Kenzo: W- what was that, Kate?

03:31:31.590 --> 03:31:33.150
Kenzo: Or what was that, Riswynn?

03:31:33.150 --> 03:31:37.030
Riswynn: I, I reach a w- a waterskin towards you in case you, uh-

03:31:37.030 --> 03:31:37.850
Kenzo: Ah

03:31:37.850 --> 03:31:42.610
Riswynn: ... are coming back into a physical state where you need some refreshment.

03:31:42.610 --> 03:31:50.909
Kenzo: Yeah, Kenzo kind of looks up, looks up at, at, um, at, uh, you and is, you know, is very grateful, you know, grabs some water, um, drinks.

03:31:52.170 --> 03:31:52.810
Kenzo: Thank you, friend.

03:31:54.330 --> 03:31:55.590
Kenzo: I think you helped save my life.

03:31:58.270 --> 03:32:00.030
Riswynn: Well, we all contributed.

03:32:01.570 --> 03:32:02.010
Riswynn: You're welcome.

03:32:07.190 --> 03:32:09.130
Seeker: Well, we're glad to have you back, Kenzo.

03:32:11.290 --> 03:32:11.520
Kenzo: Well, thank y-

03:32:11.520 --> 03:32:12.130
Seeker: I'll admit...

03:32:13.290 --> 03:32:14.290
Seeker: Say again, sorry.

03:32:14.290 --> 03:32:16.670
Kenzo: Oh, go ahead, go ahead. Finish what you were saying, Seeker.

03:32:16.670 --> 03:32:20.990
Seeker: Oh, I admit I'm curious, based on my,

03:32:22.270 --> 03:32:23.990
Seeker: as you know, geological interests,

03:32:25.270 --> 03:32:30.870
Seeker: uh, how it was that you were able to shake the ground around you, if indeed you were causing that somehow.

03:32:32.550 --> 03:32:33.750
Kenzo: The ground was shaking around me?

03:32:35.250 --> 03:32:36.490
Riswynn: Oh, yes.

03:32:36.490 --> 03:32:38.870
Seeker: So it seemed while you were meditating earlier,

03:32:40.670 --> 03:32:42.370
Seeker: or it looked like you were meditating.

03:32:47.170 --> 03:32:51.830
Kenzo: I think I need, I think I need, uh, to spend the evening processing what has occurred,

03:32:53.150 --> 03:32:56.690
Kenzo: but what were these things, you know?

03:32:56.690 --> 03:32:58.590
Kenzo: Where are they now, those creatures?

03:32:58.590 --> 03:33:01.570
Kenzo: Like, I just kinda, like, look at, like, like, I'm a- I'm shredded.

03:33:01.570 --> 03:33:03.370
Kenzo: [laughs] You know what I mean? It's like I'm just, like, like, like-

03:33:03.370 --> 03:33:03.810
Seeker: Yeah

03:33:03.810 --> 03:33:05.390
Kenzo: ... just been a shredded, you know.

03:33:05.390 --> 03:33:07.050
Seeker: You took a lot of bites.

03:33:07.050 --> 03:33:08.790
Kenzo: What, what were those things?

03:33:08.790 --> 03:33:09.530
Kenzo: What the hell was that?

03:33:13.170 --> 03:33:15.310
Delwath: I think they were creatures from some other world.

03:33:16.570 --> 03:33:20.570
Seeker: These, these mouth creatures, I've seen a drawing of them in a book.

03:33:20.570 --> 03:33:26.870
Seeker: Many years ago, well, actually, it's not that many years ago, [laughs] I, I read a book about-

03:33:26.870 --> 03:33:28.100
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah, not that long

03:33:28.100 --> 03:33:30.450
Seeker: ... about creatures that can come

03:33:31.650 --> 03:33:35.030
Seeker: from darker planes of, than this one.

03:33:36.230 --> 03:33:40.490
Seeker: But they have to have been summoned here somehow by powerful magic

03:33:43.880 --> 03:33:44.880
Kenzo: This is, um...

03:33:46.100 --> 03:33:54.600
Kenzo: You know, as, as kind of Kenzo's, like, talking and drinking, you can see, like, like, kind of, um, and in a way kind of like coming out of his trance a little bit.

03:33:54.600 --> 03:34:02.860
Kenzo: It, it's like his eyes start changing back to normal, the normal color from before, and he sort of just kind of getting back into himself, and he's like,

03:34:05.200 --> 03:34:05.620
Kenzo: "Um,

03:34:07.420 --> 03:34:10.670
Kenzo: this... I, I don't know what this means, but this is, this is,

03:34:12.660 --> 03:34:13.160
Kenzo: uh,

03:34:14.960 --> 03:34:15.980
Kenzo: I... This, this is...

03:34:17.980 --> 03:34:21.900
Kenzo: It's s- it's, um, hard to process everything that's happening right now,

03:34:23.400 --> 03:34:24.680
Kenzo: what the implications of this are."

03:34:26.580 --> 03:34:29.520
Seeker: Indeed. Well, we have a journey ahead of us to puzzle things out.

03:34:37.120 --> 03:34:39.900
Kenzo: What are, what are your plans for the evening to prepare?

03:34:43.800 --> 03:34:44.520
Seeker: W- uh,

03:34:46.020 --> 03:34:52.000
Seeker: well, uh, I think, I think I showed you my, um, the little booklet, uh, my humble,

03:34:53.060 --> 03:35:00.020
Seeker: uh, sheaf of drawings that I've now bound up into Legendary Staff of Kenzo, my account of your feats in the games.

03:35:00.020 --> 03:35:00.270
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:35:00.270 --> 03:35:03.720
Seeker: Uh, I was thinking I might spend a few hours tonight, uh, drawing.

03:35:04.980 --> 03:35:08.860
DM: Eric, I think at some point I'm gonna actually need to see the Legendary Staff of Kenzo,

03:35:10.120 --> 03:35:11.640
DM: like, in real life.

03:35:11.640 --> 03:35:12.180
Seeker: [laughs]

03:35:12.180 --> 03:35:12.520
Kenzo: Okay.

03:35:12.520 --> 03:35:14.260
Seeker: I'll, I'll, I'll work on it.

03:35:14.260 --> 03:35:18.420
Seeker: I did actually just destroy the binding earlier today, so let's put that back together.

03:35:18.420 --> 03:35:18.580
Seeker: Um,

03:35:21.100 --> 03:35:22.520
Seeker: yeah, so I'm gonna make some drawings.

03:35:25.840 --> 03:35:27.660
Seeker: I think we all need to get some rest.

03:35:27.660 --> 03:35:27.840
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:35:28.860 --> 03:35:30.460
Kenzo: I think that's right.

03:35:30.460 --> 03:35:30.700
Kenzo: Um,

03:35:31.880 --> 03:35:35.420
Kenzo: Tim, am I... Would it be easier for me to, like, find a new, new clothing someplace?

03:35:36.920 --> 03:35:40.760
DM: Yeah. I mean, you probably have a spare set of clothing anyway.

03:35:40.760 --> 03:35:42.250
Kenzo: Yeah, spare set of clothing.

03:35:42.250 --> 03:35:42.660
Kenzo: Perfect.

03:35:44.240 --> 03:35:48.700
Delwath: I'm gonna just, before it gets too late, look around and see if there's any tracks.

03:35:49.840 --> 03:35:50.280
Seeker: Oh, yeah.

03:35:51.980 --> 03:35:53.439
DM: Uh, okay.

03:35:53.440 --> 03:35:54.580
DM: Uh, make a survival check.

03:35:57.240 --> 03:35:57.920
Delwath: With a six.

03:36:04.740 --> 03:36:05.280
Delwath: 23.

03:36:07.420 --> 03:36:12.680
DM: Um, yeah, there are tracks leading north, and you can distinguish the, uh,

03:36:13.920 --> 03:36:15.460
DM: the hyena creatures and the

03:36:16.600 --> 03:36:27.460
DM: moths. They seem to have come together traveling from the north, but then split, um, when they hit this building, and the moths went, uh,

03:36:27.460 --> 03:36:31.320
DM: right, and the hyena creatures went left.

03:36:31.320 --> 03:36:32.540
Delwath: What time of day is it?

03:36:33.980 --> 03:36:36.120
DM: Evening now. The sun is setting.

03:36:36.120 --> 03:36:36.560
Delwath: Oh, okay.

03:36:39.140 --> 03:36:41.140
Seeker: I wonder what those moth guys were headed towards.

03:36:42.700 --> 03:36:46.540
DM: But you can see... I mean, you can get a read on where the tracks are leading, and-

03:36:46.540 --> 03:36:47.200
Delwath: Right

03:36:47.200 --> 03:36:51.580
DM: ... um, you know, you're pretty sure you can pick up the trail in the morning, unless it...

03:36:51.580 --> 03:36:53.990
DM: If it rains overnight or something, that would be bad.

03:36:53.990 --> 03:36:54.510
Delwath: Right. Right, right.

03:36:54.510 --> 03:36:56.100
DM: But it almost never rains, so.

03:36:56.100 --> 03:36:57.220
Delwath: Right. Right. Okay.

03:36:57.220 --> 03:36:59.219
DM: It's a desert.

03:36:59.220 --> 03:36:59.780
Delwath: Yep.

03:36:59.780 --> 03:37:00.400
DM: Yeah.

03:37:02.600 --> 03:37:03.220
Kenzo: All right.

03:37:03.220 --> 03:37:03.240
DM: Okay.

03:37:03.240 --> 03:37:07.080
Kenzo: I'm just gonna get a change of clothes and then go meditate at the oasis tonight.

03:37:07.080 --> 03:37:07.460
DM: Okay.

03:37:11.800 --> 03:37:15.980
DM: Okay, so as you all settle into your evening,

03:37:17.520 --> 03:37:19.320
DM: preparing for your journey in the morning,

03:37:20.540 --> 03:37:20.740
DM: um,

03:37:23.360 --> 03:37:33.520
DM: quiet settles over the town, interrupted by the sort of clangs and, uh, sort of bustling noises of horses being packed, of,

03:37:33.520 --> 03:37:33.780
DM: of

03:37:34.900 --> 03:37:39.480
DM: saddles be- saddlebags being loaded, food stores being emptied out of the inn.

03:37:41.020 --> 03:37:46.600
DM: And when you wake at first light in the morning, a h- a huge, uh,

03:37:49.020 --> 03:37:54.540
DM: a huge horde has gathered, probably 1,000 people or so, on

03:37:56.140 --> 03:38:02.970
DM: at least 1,500 horses, sort of stretching to the west as people begin to, um,

03:38:04.560 --> 03:38:07.580
DM: head out of the village for safety.

03:38:07.580 --> 03:38:14.320
DM: Um, some moving quickly ahead, some, like the halflings, moving a bit slower behind.

03:38:14.320 --> 03:38:25.120
DM: Um, but Havdar and about 25 troops that he's managed to recruit here, as well as the survivors of the, um, retreat of the refugees,

03:38:25.120 --> 03:38:27.180
DM: uh, keeping a close watch on the rear.

03:38:28.900 --> 03:38:31.700
DM: And as the town empties to the west,

03:38:32.720 --> 03:38:33.340
DM: you turn,

03:38:35.060 --> 03:38:38.060
DM: looking north to your destination, um,

03:38:39.520 --> 03:38:46.020
DM: the rising sun casting long shadows as you pick up the tracks again and begin to head north.

03:38:47.240 --> 03:38:48.760
DM: And that is where we'll stop for tonight.

03:38:50.480 --> 03:38:51.120
Seeker: Awesome.

03:38:53.420 --> 03:38:53.460
Kenzo: Awesome.

03:38:53.460 --> 03:38:53.930
Seeker: Thanks, Tim.

03:38:53.930 --> 03:38:54.280
DM: Sounds good.

03:38:54.280 --> 03:38:54.760
Seeker: Thanks for join-
